# Optional provider credentials. Never place a value after an inline comment.
# credentials.demo.env (committed) supplies public demo keys for EIA, Congress.gov and EODHD and is
# loaded first; a key set here overrides it. Leave a demo-covered line commented out to keep
# the demo value: an empty value (NAME=) here would override the demo key with nothing.
FRED_API_KEY=
# EIA_API_KEY=
# SEC requires an identifying user agent; use your own contact information.
SEC_USER_AGENT=

# Additional credentials for providers included in this Episode 1 build.
BLS_API_KEY=
NASDAQ_API_KEY=
CFTC_APP_TOKEN=
# CONGRESS_GOV_API_KEY=

# EODHD (v9, both API images): your own eodhd.com API token for obb.eodhd.* and
# /api/v1/eodhd/*. Commented out, credentials.demo.env's "demo" token applies, which
# covers only EODHD's demo symbols; other symbols are refused. Nothing else changes.
# EODHD_API_KEY=

# live-grid (v10, the opt-in `live` profile) reads EODHD_API_KEY above for its websocket
# quotes and REST seed (websockets need a paid EODHD plan) and the OPENBB_API_* pair below.
# The Subscriptions iframe widget is named by the address each request used (through the
# gateway, /grid/subscriptions). docker-compose.yml passes LIVE_GRID_PUBLIC_URL to live-grid,
# empty by default; set it in .env, not here, only to pin one address for every client. A direct
# HTTPS tailnet Serve to live-grid MUST set it to that https:// address, or the iframe URL comes
# out http:// and the page's writes get 403 (Origin mismatch). The
# kdb+ licence is a file, not a value: put your own kc.lic in ./kdb-license/ (git-ignored).
# Left empty: the compose value wins over this file.
LIVE_GRID_PUBLIC_URL=

# API Basic auth. Leave OPENBB_API_AUTH empty to keep the API open (no BDOBB
# settings API). Set it to true and fill both values to require the credential
# on every data route and to serve BDOBB key-mode settings (GET /pro/user,
# POST /pro/display-settings). /widgets.json and /apps.json stay open.
OPENBB_API_AUTH=
OPENBB_API_USERNAME=
OPENBB_API_PASSWORD=
